# No Cursor commit trailers or authorship

When you create commits, edit messages, or suggest `git commit` text (including multi-line bodies):

- Do **not** include `Made-with: Cursor` or any line starting with `Made-with:`.
- Do **not** add `Co-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>` or similar IDE-generated `Co-authored-by` trailers.
- Do **not** set Author or Committer to `Cursor Agent`, `cursoragent`, `cursoragent@cursor.com`, or `cursor@cursor.com`. Commit as the repository user.
- If the tool or environment inserts those lines or that identity, **remove them** before the commit is finalized.

Prefer the repo’s `prepare-commit-msg` hook when documented (`git config core.hooksPath .githooks`). Repos that enforce this in CI will fail merges if those lines or that identity appear in **any** commit in the pull request or in the pushed batch (including default squash text that repeats commit bodies, and GitHub contributor credit from Author/Committer).
